			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule to e792634e04de\n\nUpdate Element from 991e3b3 to e792634e, pulling in upstream Cocoon extension host runtime improvements.\n\nThis sync brings the latest Cocoon submodule state (cb1a388) into the Land build, ensuring the extension host has access to recent runtime changes.",
			"SHA": "83083f528b4c94eb04130b730863979183254a87"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T16:46:17Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				5214,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Expand trusted paths and add executable magic-number detection\n\nSubmodule sync bringing three complementary improvements for extension runtime reliability:\n1. **Extended trusted paths** (`PathSecurity.rs`): Add `/tmp`, `/private/tmp`, `/var/tmp` for language servers (ruby-lsp, pyright, etc.), third-party tool state (`~/.gitkraken`, `~/.copilot`, `~/.config/git`), and read-only POSIX OS files.\n2. **Magic-number executable detection** (`VsixInstaller.rs`): Probe file headers for ELF, Mach-O fat/thin, and shebang. Detect bin paths (`bin/`, `server/`, `tools/`, `omnisharp`, `adapter`, `native`) and promote 0o644 → 0o755 for detected executables, fixing EACCES on spawn. Add `HealExecutableBits()` for retroactive fixes.\n3. **Boot-time exec-bit heal** (`Scanner.rs`): Walk user extensions (`~/.land/extensions/`) at scan time to recover extensions installed before the fix.\n\nImpact: Extension binaries (rust-analyzer, GitLens, Copilot) that were failing with EACCES due to missing exec bits now run correctly.",
			"SHA": "6df08625901c15474baf39bc8680dd4bc9ae9dd6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T15:38:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				5214,
				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(Land): Enable native file watcher and add VS Code API coverage matrix\n\nSynchronize Element submodule to pull in Mountain-native search provider integration and PostHog exception cap. This commit also introduces comprehensive VS Code API documentation and enables Layer4 file watching.\n\nChanges:\n- **Search Provider (Element):** New land-native ISearchService implementation in Sky and Output that routes Search viewlet queries to Mountain's `search:findFiles` / `search:findInFiles` handlers. Resolves silent zero-result returns when filesystem is Mountain-based.\n- **PostHog Cap:** Add `LAND_POSTHOG_SKY_EXCEPTION_GLOBAL_LIMIT` (default 7) to respect CDN's ~10/10s ceiling and prevent rate-limit warnings during boot flurries.\n- **File Watcher:** Change `TierFileWatcher` from `Stub` to `Layer4`, enabling Mountain's native notify-crate backend (FSEvents/inotify/ReadDirectoryChangesW). This unblocks LSP-driven extensions from receiving disk mutation events.\n- **Documentation:** Add VSCode-API-Coverage-Matrix.md - a 419-line authoritative map of every `vscode.*` namespace, implementation track (Stock-Node/Rust-native), status, and planned migrations.\n\nImpact: Search now works with Mountain filesystem. Extension file watchers (ESLint, TypeScript, Tailwind) can now receive filesystem change events. Comprehensive API tracking document enables systematic dual-track implementation.",
			"SHA": "fc2622c3a692b211f0334ca5348ec5d09accd546"
		}
	],
